  "verbalization": "Eriojaposide B is shown to interact with CD276 antigen through a multi-step mechanism involving DNA polymerase iota, which is targeted by two different compounds, Isomitraphylline and Isodactyloxene. Both of these compounds are implicated in targeting DNA polymerase iota, which in turn leads to the inhibition of CD276 antigen. The presence of a third compound, (-)-(5E,12E,2S,3S,4S,9S,11S,15R)-15-benzoyloxylathyra-5,12-dien-3-ol-14-one, further supports the notion that Eriojaposide B may act through a similar pathway, ultimately leading to the downregulation of CD276 antigen. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust, mechanistically linked relationship, with the core mechanism involving the inhibition of DNA polymerase iota, which is a key player in the regulation of CD276 antigen. The evidence supports a plausible pathway where Eriojaposide B may exert its effects by targeting DNA polymerase iota, thereby influencing CD276 antigen expression.",
